st.cljc\n M test/yin/vm/integer_test.cljc\n D test/yin/vm/linearize_test.cljc\n M test/yin/vm/linker_test.cljc\n M test/yin/vm/rule_r_test.cljc\n M test/yin/vm/semantic_engine_test.cljc\n M test/yin/vm/semantic_ffi_test.cljc\n M test/yin/vm/semantic_register/derive_test.cljc\n M test/yin/vm/semantic_register/effects_test.cljc\n M test/yin/vm/semantic_register/linearize_test.cljc\n M test/yin/vm/semantic_register/vm_test.cljc\n M test/yin/vm/semantic_stream_observer_test.cljc\n D test/yin/vm/semantic_test.cljc\n M test/yin/vm/stream_poll_test.cljc\n M test/yin/vm/telemetry_test.cljc\n M test/yin/vm/test_utils.cljc\n M test/yin/vm/ucf/remote_test.cljc\n D test/yin/vm/ucf_test.cljc\n M test/yin/vm_test.cljc\n?? collab/1792050511876-architect-8f1-ruling.report.md\n?? collab/1792052228000-architect-8f1-review.report.md\n?? collab/1792053792008-engineer-8f3.report.md\n?? collab/1792055212830-architect-8f3-review.report.md\n?? collab/1792055987000-reviewer-8f3-glm.report.md\n?? collab/1792056067234-engineer-8f3b.report.md\n?? collab/1792560000000-architect-phase8-plan.report.md\n?? collab/1793050000000-engineer-8f3.gpt-6.1-sol.stdout.log\n?? collab/1793050000000-engineer-8f3.prompt.md\n?? collab/1793060000000-architect-8f3-review.fable.stdout.log\n?? collab/1793060000000-architect-8f3-review.prompt.md\n?? collab/1793060000000-reviewer-8f3-glm.prompt.md\n?? collab/1793060000000-reviewer-8f3-glm.stdout.log\n?? collab/1793070000000-engineer-8f3b.gpt-6.1-sol.stdout.log\n?? collab/1793070000000-engineer-8f3b.prompt.md\n?? collab/1793080000000-engineer-8f3c.gpt-6.1-sol.stdout.log\n?? collab/1793080000000-engineer-8f3c.prompt.md\nCompleted-GMT: 2026-10-15 09:19:47 GMT\nCompleted-Local: 2026-10-15 16:19:47 +07\nCoding-Agent: glm (glm-5.3)\nSession-ID: pending (harness does not expose it)\n\n# 8f-3 supplementary parity audit (reviewer, GLM)\n\nTree: srvm-phase8f3 @ c55a6ceb + the uncommitted 8f-3 diff. Read-only except this report. The engineer's ledger (collab/1792053792008-engineer-8f3.report.md) was read but every claim below was re-derived from `git show HEAD:…`, the worktree files, and fresh test runs.\n\n## What I verified independently\n\n- **Deftest census.** Per-file `file:deftest-name` sets, HEAD vs worktree: removed = exactly the 81 deftests of the four deleted files (semantic 24, linearize 22, code 12, ucf 23); added = exactly 16 (15 carried-over forms in semantic_register/{vm,linearize}_test + 1 new demo contract regression). No deftest in any surviving file was deleted or renamed. My raw token count `(deftest` over test/ is 4419 → 4354 (−65 = −81 + 16), matching the engineer's 4418 → 4353 up to a one-off regex difference on their side; the delta is identical.\n- **Fresh runs (JVM, this tree).** `yin.vm.semantic-register.vm-test` + `linearize-test`: 48 tests / 1302 assertions, 0 failures. `effects-test` + `datomworld.demo.continuation-handoff-test` + `semantic-register.code-test`: 60 / 386, 0 failures. `semantic-engine-test` + `semantic-ffi-test` + `semantic-stream-observer-test` + `semantic-register.load-paths-test`: 35 / 291, 0 failures. Kondo over src+test: 27 errors / 63 warnings, all in cljd/Dart-host files untouched by this diff — no new diagnostics from the changed files.\n- **No loop-over-zero / vacuous passes.** Iterated corpora are non-empty and mostly self-guarding: `code-test/refusals` 33 rows over 16 rules with `every-item-has-a-refusal-row` asserting items 1–13 ∪ {3,4} and `(= 14 (count code/rules))`; `corpus/programs` 32 entries with `corpus-is-large-enough` asserting ≥ 25 and keys = goldens (scan_test independently asserts 32); `malformed-row-sets` 14 entries; rule_r `loaders` 6 legs; the new demo stamp test iterates 2 fields × 2 stamps. The ported consumer hunks change loaders/keys only; I found no removed or loosened `is` in any of them (semantic_engine/ffi/stream_observer, test_utils, ucf/remote_test, the nine C4 files, both demos, query_test, telemetry, engine_gate, ffi, responder, attach_image, heap_reclamation, host_typed_values, debruijn/*, cell/data/integer/effect_forgery, linker prose, bench).\n\n## Deleted-deftest verdicts (81)\n\nVerdict key: CONFIRMED = surviving test read, fact retained (adapted to the register payload where the payload itself changed). RETIRED-OK = solely about the deleted v3 representation (v3 stack-bytecode layout, v3 segment/datom batches, v3 API). WEAKER = fact partially retained.\n\n### semantic_test.cljc (24)\n\n| Deleted deftest | Verdict | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| create-vm-test | CONFIRMED | vm_test/create-vm-test: same 3 FFI-pair resources, empty code/env, nil control/continuation, halted; `:in-stream` refusal via `some? ex-data` instead of `thrown?` — equivalent. |\n| load-image-decodes-refs-and-opcodes-test | RETIRED-OK + covered | v3 mnemonic→opcode/ref decode; v4 image contract pinned by vm_test/image-shape (keys, vector, analysis, address, alias, control pc 0, length, no `:stack`). |\n| load-image-rejects-ill-formed-batches-test | CONFIRMED | loader-refusals-are-the-validators iterates the 33-row exact-defect corpus; code_test/refusal-rows-name-rule-and-pc. |\n| load-image-verifies-a-claimed-address-test | CONFIRMED | mint_test/fetch-refuses-bad-content (absent address; correctly-hashed malformed vector refused `:target-bounds`); computed address + alias in image-shape. The v3 `:yin.code/hash` claim mechanism is representation. |\n| load-vector-decodes-and-aliases-test | CONFIRMED | image-shape + segment-ids + load_paths/both-paths-one-image; runs-to-11 via closure-call-test. |\n| load-vector-mints-below-the-loaded-floor-test | CONFIRMED | segment-ids `( (< (:program b) floor))`; attach_image/semantic-attach-mints… (fresh local id, alias, below held ids). Literal −16 retired (counted v3 rows). |\n| load-vector-refuses-malformed-vectors-test | CONFIRMED | loader-refusals-are-the-validators (exact defects, 33 rows). |\n| live-id-conflict-fires-on-the-direct-path-test | CONFIRMED | segment-ids: \"already holds different code\" refusal + identical reload accepted. |\n| arithmetic-test | CONFIRMED | vm_test/arithmetic-test (3, 12). |\n| closure-call-test | CONFIRMED | vm_test/closure-call-test (11, halted, nil continuation; 15 nested capture). |\n| under-arity-call-binds-missing-param-to-nil-test | CONFIRMED | same name, nil under outer y=10. |\n| over-arity-call-drops-extra-args-test | CONFIRMED | same name, 5 with extra 99. |\n| branch-false-test | CONFIRMED | same name, 1/2/2 for true/false/nil. |\n| store-and-gensym-test | CONFIRMED | same name, 5/`:id-0`/`:g-2` via AST effect nodes. |\n| tail-countdown-test | CONFIRMED | tail-countdown (10⁵, every step k≤1, \"done\") + tail-countdown-test (1 vs 1001 frames, resume/unwind); pc=17/`:stack []` literals are v3 representation; saved-window rules pinned by effects_test/saved-window-membership. |\n| park-resume-test | CONFIRMED | effects_test/park-resume: exact parked record (identity, saved window, deliver), EDN round-trip, resume clears `:parked`, unknown-id \"not found\". |\n| segment-id-is-stable-test | CONFIRMED | segment-ids (refusal + reload) + attach_image/semantic-parked-entry-restores… (ids never renumbered, parked entry wakes into its own code). |\n| current-continuation-test | CONFIRMED | reified-shape (exact payload + EDN), continuation-restores-captured-environment (walker/register trace equality), return-frame-shape, continuation-invoke tests. pc=7/`:stack-base` are v3 payload shape. |\n| step-test | CONFIRMED | one-step-one-write (pc 0→1, exactly one register write), halt-shape, ready-for-ingress; idle-VM-steps-to-itself pinned on the register machine by observer `an-idle-step-waits-for-the-observer-test` (full machine equality); run-to-11 via closure-call-test. |\n| reset-test | WEAKER | attach-load-ast-and-reset pins window `{}`, nil value, code preserved (and free-environment-retention pins free-env), but the old assertions `control = {:segment s :pc 0}` and \"rerun → 11\" have no semantic-register successor (native debruijn register VM pins pc-0 for its own backend only). See P3-1. |\n| blocked-stream-next-wakes-test | CONFIRMED | engine an-empty-stream-parks-the-reader + a-value-wakes…; effects wake-delivers-to-rd; resume-pc = blocked-pc+1 pinned by blocked-read-entry-shape. |\n| blocked-entries-are-pure-data-test | CONFIRMED | blocked-read-entry-shape (exact entry + EDN round-trip + wake), blocked-put (`:put`, `:datom` retry value), terminal-wake-raises (parked wake errors exactly like the immediate put), stream-outcomes-and-edn-wake. Minor composite gap: see P3-3. |\n| ffi-call-test | CONFIRMED | effects ffi-sent (entry shape, call-id, bridge answer, `[nil 7 2]`, `:parked` empty) + bridge-installed-handlers-round-trip. |\n| semantic-restore-retained-response-route-test | CONFIRMED | effects retained-response-route: fixed vs carried response keys, parked identity untouched, both legs; wait `:reason`/`:call-id` facts live in ffi-retained. |\n\n### linearize_test.cljc (22)\n\n| Deleted deftest | Verdict | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| lowered-segments-are-well-formed | CONFIRMED | goldens-are-well-formed over all 32 corpus programs. |\n| pcs-are-dense | CONFIRMED | provenance-is-one-row-per-pc: counts equal, pcs exactly `(range n)` in order. |\n| every-ref-resolves | CONFIRMED | v4 target admission: code_test refusals (`:target-bounds`, `:body-partition` incl. jump-into-body) + golden acceptance; tempid-collision fact is v3 representation. |\n| every-instruction-has-a-source | CONFIRMED | provenance count equality + every datom-lane source is an AST entity. |\n| worked-example-matches-the-design | CONFIRMED | worked-example-is-byte-for-byte-the-design (exact vector, address, tail-flag variant). |\n| if-lowers-to-branch-and-jump | CONFIRMED | the `:if`-family goldens are pinned byte-for-byte by row-lane and datom-lane matches; behavior by vm_test/branch-arms-share-rd. |\n| options-set-t-and-segment-id | RETIRED-OK | v3 instruction-datom t/tempid stamping; v4 projection emits a vector. |\n| id-start-is-validated-over-the-whole-range | RETIRED-OK | v3 tempid allocation range. |\n| id-range-stays-within-host-safe-integers | RETIRED-OK | v3 generated entity ids; no v4 counterpart exists. |\n| literals-are-opaque-data | CONFIRMED | same-name survivor, same opaque-equality assertions. |\n| host-values-are-rejected-naming-the-node | CONFIRMED | same-name survivor: same 4 nested shapes, exact `:node`/`:field` (`:value`/`:val`), metadata survival, symbolic primitive. |\n| unsupported-nodes-are-rejected-naming-the-node | CONFIRMED | same-name survivor: exact `{:type,:node}` for datom nodes, unknown tag via `:id`; map/row refusals in unsupported-and-reserved… and malformed-row-sets-are-refused. Old map-input nested case is reached through the datom lane now (map ASTs encode to `:yin/type` datoms); exact-payload refusal retained. |\n| ast-loader-lowers-before-loading | CONFIRMED | rule_r the-lowering-adapters-verify-the-incoming-stamp (`:contract-missing`/`:contract-mismatch` before lowering; current stamp loads and runs 3) + every-persistent-code-loader… (6 loader legs) + load_paths (row/datom agreement). |\n| evaluation-order-matches-the-walker | CONFIRMED | same-name survivor, now against real register execution; exact 9-entry log + 11. |\n| lower-rows-worked-example-matches-the-design | CONFIRMED | worked-example + row-lane-matches-the-goldens (all programs, exact vector+address). |\n| lower-rows-provenance-is-one-row-per-pc-keyed-by-occurrence | CONFIRMED (one sub-fact weaker) | provenance-is-one-row-per-pc + shared-occurrences-expand-positionally (distinct occurrence paths). The old \"a bare row set has no source occurrence\" (nil origin slot) is no longer asserted — see P3-2. |\n| lower-rows-rejects-incomplete-source-occurrence-identities | CONFIRMED | same-name survivor, same six origins, exact `:origin` rule. |\n| lower-envelope-stamps-the-selected-member-source-origin | CONFIRMED | test_utils/run-encoder-session selects the envelope member, bounds-validates (`:batch-envelope`) and stamps `vm/source-origin`; exercised end-to-end by observer the-two-observer-stages-compose (envelope block) and source-envelope-projects-occurrence-side-tables (unchanged); origin/root identity in provenance-is-one-row-per-pc. Production envelope validation (encoder.cljc, unchanged) keeps its own `:batch-envelope` refusals. |\n| lower-rows-provenance-paths-resolve-to-the-emitting-node | CONFIRMED | same-name survivor, same corpus ∪ parity/corpus, same count/path/occurrence-join/emitting-tag assertions. |\n| lower-rows-vector-decodes-to-the-datom-path-image | CONFIRMED | load_paths both-paths-one-image + round-tripped-rows-load-to-the-same-image (v3 `load-image` API retired). |\n| lower-rows-rejects-malformed-row-sets | CONFIRMED | malformed-row-sets-are-refused + observer a-malformed-row-set-is-rejected… ; exact per-rule defects pinned at the row-validator level by vm_test/malformed-row-sets-each-name-exactly-their-own-rule (the old test also only asserted `thrown?`). |\n| lower-rows-evaluation-order-matches-the-walker | CONFIRMED | same-name survivor, log equality + 11 against real execution. |\n\n### code_test.cljc (12)\n\nAll RETIRED-OK with CONFIRMED v4 coverage: the ten batch/vector grammar tests pin the v3 segment-entity/attr grammar and the v3 stack-shaped vector grammar (`[:push]`, `[:call argc tail?]`, `[:closure params pc]`), both deleted per ruling R2/R5; the v4 grammar is covered at equal or greater strength by semantic_register/code_test (33 exact-defect refusal rows over 16 rules incl. the old rules' v4 twins — nonempty/mnemonic/operand-kind/saturation/target-bounds/terminator→body-partition/argc→call-operands — with the \"minimal vector passing every earlier rule\" docstring pinning rule-major precedence, and every-golden-is-accepted). The two projection tests' fact (address+pc columns prepended) survives as scan_test/segment-rows-carry-a-and-pc (exact `(into [a pc] tuple)` rows) and query_test/code-joins-store-put-key-to-ast-by-value (adapted rd-slot pattern, `#{[99]}` unchanged).\n\n### ucf_test.cljc (23)\n\nAll RETIRED-OK per Architect ruling R2 (every fixture is a hand-assembled v3 `:yin.code/*` batch run through the deleted v3 canonicalizer/safepoint half). I checked the strictness bar — no language/VM behavior is being retired as \"representation\":\n\n- The five behavioral conformance facts survive as behavior on the register kernel: explicit park (effects/park-resume), blocked read (blocked-read-entry-shape, resume pc = pc+1), blocked write (blocked-put, retry value), ffi sent (ffi-sent), ffi retained (ffi-retained: request-sent/`:put`/op/args, response resumes), effectful primitive call parking (tail-effect-returns-through-k). `transitions-cover-the-vocabulary`'s classification table itself is the deleted static half; each parking kind it named is behaviorally exercised.\n- `lexically-required`'s liveness fact survives as the saved-window rules: effects/saved-window-membership asserts the entry window is exactly `analysis/saved` at the safepoint (and excludes the destination rd); frame_test/safepoint_harness_test (unchanged) own the frame/safepoint contract.\n- Canonicalization/address facts: saturation (linearize/saturation-materializes-defaults), address identity (golden-addresses-are-the-code-address-on-this-host, code_test/load-vector-checks-the-stamp-then-the-rules), bad-content refusal (mint_test/fetch-refuses-bad-content incl. correctly-hashed `[[:jump 9]]` → `:target-bounds`).\n- The stack-shaped tables (safepoints/safepoint-table/stack-effect/parking-kinds/activation-state/stack-bases) and the v3 batch refusals/equivalence laws are v3 representation with no v4 counterpart by design (ruling R2: \"no v4 batch grammar nobody emits\").\n\n## Findings\n\n**P3-1 — reset coverage weaker than claimed (semantic_register/vm_test.cljc:74-89).** The ledger maps semantic_test/reset-test to attach-load-ast-and-reset as \"code preserved and program reruns\". Code preservation, empty window and nil value are asserted; \"program reruns\" is not — nothing on the semantic-register kernel asserts `vm/reset` restores `control` to pc 0 or that a reset machine re-runs to its value (the `(vm/eval a nil)` assertion continues a mid-run machine; the pc-0 assertion exists only on the native de Bruijn register backend, debruijn/register_test.cljc:496-499). Two `is` lines in attach-load-ast-and-reset would close it. Not a behavior change — `reset` is implemented as pc-0 control restore (semantic_register.cljc:338-339).\n\n**P3-2 — bare-row-set nil-origin slot unpinned (semantic_register/linearize_test.cljc:124-137).** The old lower-rows-provenance test asserted that a row set projected without an origin carries `nil` in the provenance origin slot; every current provenance assertion passes an explicit origin (or asserts only paths). One `(is (nil? (nth (first (:provenance (linearize/project-rows bc))) 1)))`-style line restores it.\n\n**P3-3 — writer-entry EDN round-trip composite no longer spelled out.** blocked-put wakes the original in-memory `:put` entry; the EDN round-trip-then-wake is now pinned for reader entries (engine a-wait-set-read-back-from-edn-resumes, effects stream-outcomes-and-edn-wake) and FFI wait-sets, and the `:put` carrier path is pinned by ucf.remote put-round-trips, but no test round-trips a blocked writer's wait-set through EDN and then wakes it on the register kernel. The pure-data fact itself is still pinned structurally (exact entry equality in blocked-put).\n\n**P3-4 — dead fixture (test/yin/vm/malformed_rows.cljc:54).** `malformed/malformed-vectors` lost its last consumers (semantic_test, code_test) and now has none; the v4 twin lives in semantic_register/code_test `refusals`. Harmless (unused public var, no kondo noise); drop it or leave it for 8f-2's file moves.\n\nNo P1/P2 findings: every deleted language/VM behavior fact I could identify has a same-strength successor on the new kernel, the RETIRED-OK set is v3-representation-only (and matches ruling R2/R5 exactly), the consumer ports are assertion-preserving, and the counts (81 out / 16 in, 15 carried + 1 new) are exactly as reported.\n\nREADY\n(ns yin.vm.semantic-register.vm-test\n  (:require [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n            [yin.vm :as vm]\n            [yin.vm.test-utils :as tu]\n            [yin.vm.engine :as engine]\n            [yin.vm.module :as module]\n            [yin.vm.values :as values]\n            [yin.vm.semantic-register :as sr]\n            [yin.vm.semantic-register.analysis :as analysis]\n            [yin.vm.semantic-register.code :as code]\n            [yin.vm.semantic-register.code-test :as code-test]\n            [yin.vm.semantic-register.corpus :as corpus]\n            [yin.vm.semantic-register.parity-test :as parity]))\n\n\n(defn error-data\n  [f]\n  (try (f) nil (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) e (ex-data e))))\n\n\n(defn step-n\n  [machine n]\n  (nth (iterate vm/step machine) n))\n\n\n(defn golden\n  [label]\n  (:vector (get corpus/goldens label)))\n\n\n(defn load-golden\n  [label opts]\n  (sr/load-vector (sr/create-vm opts) (golden label) code/contract))\n\n\n(deftest stamp-before-rules\n  (doseq [[stamp rule] [[nil :contract-missing] [\"v3\" :contract-mismatch]]]\n    (is (= rule (:rule (error-data #(sr/load-vector (sr/create-vm) [] stamp)))))))\n\n\n(deftest loader-refusals-are-the-validators\n  (doseq [[item expected vector] code-test/refusals]\n    (testing (str item \" \" vector)\n      (is (= expected (:defect (error-data #(sr/load-vector (sr/create-vm) vector code/contract))))))))\n\n\n(deftest image-shape\n  (let [machine (load-golden :worked-example {}) seg (:program machine)\n        image (get (:code machine) seg)]\n    (is (= #{:vector :address :bodies :analysis :segment :length} (set (keys image))))\n    (is (= (golden :worked-example) (:vector image)))\n    (is (= (analysis/analyze (:vector image)) (:analysis image)))\n    (is (= (:address (get corpus/goldens :worked-example)) (:address image)))\n    (is (= seg (get (:code-aliases machine) (:address image))))\n    (is (= {:segment seg :pc 0} (vm/control machine)))\n    (is (= {} (:window machine)))\n    (is (nil? (:k machine)))\n    (is (= 7 (:length image)))\n    (is (not (contains? machine :stack)))))\n\n\n(deftest segment-ids\n  (let [a (load-golden :literal {}) floor (vm/loaded-code-floor (:code a))\n        b (sr/load-vector a (golden :variable) code/contract)\n        reload (sr/load-vector b (golden :literal) code/contract {:id 999})]\n    (is (< (:program b) floor))\n    (is (= (:program a) (:program reload)))\n    (is (= (:code b) (:code reload)))\n    (is (re-find #\"already holds different code\"\n                 (try (sr/load-vector a (golden :variable) code/contract {:id (:program a)}) \"\"\n                      (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) e (ex-message e)))))))\n\n\n(deftest attach-load-ast-and-reset\n  (let [a (step-n (load-golden :literal {}) 1)\n        b (sr/attach-image a (golden :variable) code/contract)\n        fields [:control :program :env :window :k :value :halted? :blocked? :parked :wait-set :ready-queue]\n        reset (vm/reset b)\n        ast-loaded (sr/load-ast (sr/create-vm) (vm/ast->datoms (corpus/lit 42)) vm/ast-contract)]\n    (is (= (select-keys a fields) (select-keys b fields)))\n    (is (= 2 (count (:code b))))\n    (is (= b (sr/attach-image b (golden :variable) code/contract)))\n    (is (= {} (:window reset)))\n    (is (nil? (:value reset)))\n    (is (= (:code b) (:code reset)))\n    (is (= 42 (vm/value (vm/run ast-loaded))))\n    (is (= :contract-mismatch (:rule (error-data #(sr/load-ast (sr/create-vm) [] \"bad\")))))\n    (is (some? (error-data #(vm/eval a (corpus/lit 1)))))\n    (is (= 42 (vm/value (vm/eval a nil))))))\n\n\n(deftest one-step-one-write\n  (let [f vector machine (load-golden :worked-example {:env {'f f 'g inc 'x 1 'y 2}})\n        after (vm/step machine)]\n    (is (= {:segment (:program machine) :pc 1} (vm/control after)))\n    (is (= {1 f} (:window after)))))\n\n\n(deftest return-frame-shape\n  (let [machine (load-golden :worked-example {:env {'f vector 'x nil 'y 2}})\n        seg (:program machine)\n        c (values/closure (:owner machine) {:type :closure :params '[z] :segment seg :entry 0 :env {}})\n        machine (assoc-in machine [:env 'g] c)\n        before (step-n machine 3) after (vm/step before)\n        frame (peek (:k after))\n        saved (select-keys (:window before) (analysis/saved (get-in before [:code seg :analysis]) 4 2))]\n    (is (= 3 (get-in before [:control :pc])))\n    (is (= {:type :return :segment seg :pc 4 :env (:env before) :window saved :rd 2} frame))\n    (is (= {1 vector} (:window frame)))\n    (is (= 2 (:rd frame)))\n    (is (= {} (:window after)))))\n\n\n(deftest tail-call-grows-no-frame\n  (let [ast (corpus/app (corpus/lam '[x] (corpus/tail (corpus/app (corpus/lam '[y] (corpus/v 'y)) (corpus/v 'x)))) (corpus/lit 7))\n        before (loop [m (parity/register-machine ast)]\n                 (let [{:keys [segment pc]} (:control m) inst (nth (get-in m [:code segment :vector]) pc)]\n                   (if (and (= :call (first inst)) (nth inst 4)) m (recur (vm/step m)))))\n        after (vm/step before)]\n    (is (= 1 (count (:k before))))\n    (is (= (:k before) (:k after)))\n    (is (= {} (:window after)))\n    (is (= 7 (vm/value (vm/run after))))))\n\n\n(deftest tail-countdown\n  (let [ast (parity/then\n              (corpus/def! 'loop (corpus/lam '[n]\n                                             (corpus/if-node (corpus/app (corpus/v '=) (corpus/v 'n) (corpus/lit 0))\n                                                             (corpus/lit \"done\")\n                                                             (corpus/tail (corpus/app (corpus/v 'loop)\n                                                                                      (corpus/app (corpus/v '-) (corpus/v 'n) (corpus/lit 1)))))))\n              (corpus/tail (corpus/app (corpus/v 'loop) (corpus/lit 100000))))\n        ;; Observe every instruction so the bound includes every closure entry.\n        bounded? (atom true)\n        machine (parity/register-machine ast)\n        result (loop [m machine]\n                 (if (vm/halted? m) m\n                     (let [next-state (vm/step m)]\n                       (when (> (count (:k next-state)) 1) (reset! bounded? false))\n                       (recur next-state))))]\n    (is @bounded?)\n    (is (= \"done\" (vm/value result)))\n    (is (vm/halted? result))\n    (is (nil? (:k result)))))\n\n\n(deftest return-writes-rd-once\n  (let [ast (corpus/app (corpus/v 'f)\n                        (corpus/app (corpus/lam '[z] (corpus/app (corpus/v 'g) (corpus/v 'z)))\n                                    (corpus/v 'x))\n                        (corpus/v 'y))\n        m (parity/register-machine ast {:env {'f vector 'g identity 'x nil 'y 2}})\n        before (loop [m m]\n                 (let [{:keys [segment pc]} (:control m)]\n                   (if (= :return (first (nth (get-in m [:code segment :vector]) pc))) m (recur (vm/step m)))))\n        {:keys [segment pc]} (:control before)\n        result-reg (second (nth (get-in before [:code segment :vector]) pc))\n        frame (peek (:k before))\n        v (get (:window before) result-reg)\n        after (vm/step before)]\n    (is (= {1 vector} (:window frame)))\n    (is (= 2 (:rd frame)))\n    (is (= 0 result-reg))\n    (is (not= (:rd frame) result-reg))\n    (is (= {1 identity 2 nil 0 nil} (:window before)))\n    (is (> (count (:window before)) 1))\n    (is (nil? v))\n    (is (= (assoc (:window frame) (:rd frame) v) (:window after)))\n    (is (= (:window frame) (dissoc (:window after) (:rd frame))))\n    (is (contains? (:window after) (:rd frame)))\n    (is (nil? (get (:window after) (:rd frame))))\n    (is (nil? (:k after)))\n    (is (= [nil 2] (vm/value (vm/run after))))))\n\n\n(deftest halt-shape\n  (doseq [vector [[[:const 0 nil] [:halt 0]] [[:const 0 false] [:halt 0]]]]\n    (let [m (sr/load-vector (sr/create-vm) vector code/contract)\n          m (assoc m :env {engine/store-of-key 'module 'x 1}) after (vm/run m)]\n      (is (nil? (:control after))) (is (nil? (:k after)))\n      (is (:halted? after)) (is (vm/halted? after))\n      (is (= (nth (first vector) 2) (:value after)))\n      (is (= {'x 1} (:env after))) (is (= {} (:window after)))))\n  (let [ast (corpus/tail (corpus/app (corpus/lam '[] (corpus/lit 8))))\n        result (vm/run (parity/register-machine ast {:env {engine/store-of-key 'module 'x 1}}))]\n    (is (= 8 (:value result)))\n    (is (nil? (:control result)))\n    (is (nil? (:k result)))\n    (is (vm/halted? result))\n    (is (= {'x 1} (:env result))))\n  (let [m (sr/create-vm) after (sr/register-restore (assoc m :env {engine/store-of-key 'm 'x 1})\n                                                    {:k nil :deliver {:deliver :return}} 9)]\n    (is (= 9 (:value after))) (is (= {'x 1} (:env after))) (is (vm/halted? after))))\n\n\n(deftest tail-primitive-returns-through-k\n  (let [ast (corpus/tail (corpus/app (corpus/lam '[n] (corpus/tail (corpus/app (corpus/v '+) (corpus/v 'n) (corpus/lit 1)))) (corpus/lit 1)))\n        states (loop [m (parity/register-machine ast) states []]\n                 (if (vm/halted? m) (conj states m) (recur (vm/step m) (conj states m))))\n        body-start (get-in (first states) [:code (:program (first states)) :bodies 1 :start])]\n    (is (= 2 (vm/value (peek states))))\n    (is (every? #(not (contains? (:window %) 0))\n                (filter #(and (:control %) (>= (get-in % [:control :pc]) body-start)) states)))))\n\n\n(deftest define-routes-to-the-module-store\n  (let [ast (corpus/app (corpus/lam '[] (corpus/def! 'answer (corpus/lit 42))))\n        machine (parity/register-machine ast {:env {engine/store-of-key 'foo}})\n        result (vm/run machine)]\n    (is (= 42 (vm/value result)))\n    (is (= 42 (get-in result [:module-stores 'foo 'answer])))\n    (is (not (contains? (:store result) 'answer)))))\n\n\n(deftest branch-arms-share-rd\n  (doseq [[label env expected rd] [[:if {'c nil} 2 0] [:if {'c false} 2 0] [:if {'c true} 1 0]\n                                   [:nested-if-same-rd {'a true 'b false 'c false} 2 0]\n                                   [:nested-if-same-rd {'a false 'b false 'c true} 3 0]\n                                   [:if-operand {'f vector 'c false 'y 9} [2 9] 2]\n                                   [:if-operand {'f vector 'c true 'y 9} [1 9] 2]]]\n    (testing label\n      (let [states (loop [m (load-golden label {:env env}) states []]\n                     (if (vm/halted? m) (conj states m) (recur (vm/step m) (conj states m))))\n            writes (keep #(when (contains? (:window %) rd) (get (:window %) rd)) states)]\n        (is (= expected (vm/value (peek states))))\n        (is (seq writes))\n        (is (= (if (= :if-operand label) (first expected) expected) (first writes)))\n        (when (= :if-operand label) (is (= (first expected) (first writes)))))))\n  (let [m (load-golden :if-in-tail {:env {'loop identity}})\n        before (loop [m m]\n                 (let [{:keys [segment pc]} (:control m) inst (nth (get-in m [:code segment :vector]) pc)]\n                   (if (and (= :call (first inst)) (nth inst 4)) m (recur (vm/step m)))))]\n    (is (= #{1 2 3 4 5 6 7 8 9} (set (keys (:window before)))))\n    (is (= [5 7 8 9 6]\n           (mapv second (filter #(contains? #{:var :const :call} (first %))\n                                (subvec (golden :if-in-tail) 11 16)))))))\n\n\n(deftest application-refusals\n  (let [ast (corpus/app (corpus/v 'f)) m (parity/register-machine ast {:env {'f 3}})\n        foreign (values/closure :other-owner {:type :closure :params [] :entry 0 :segment (:program m) :env {}})]\n    (is (= :not-applicable (:reason (error-data #(vm/run m)))))\n    (is (= {:reason :foreign-value :kind :closure}\n           (select-keys (error-data #(vm/run (assoc-in m [:env 'f] foreign))) [:reason :kind])))))\n\n\n(deftest ready-for-ingress\n  (is (engine/ready-for-ingress? (sr/create-vm)))\n  (is (engine/ready-for-ingress? (vm/run (load-golden :literal {})))))\n\n\n(deftest restore-delivery\n  (let [base (sr/create-vm) frame {:type :return :segment -1 :pc 3 :env {'x 1} :window {1 nil} :rd 2}\n        rd (sr/register-restore base {:segment -1 :pc 4 :env {} :window {1 nil} :k nil :deliver {:deliver :rd :rd 0}} false)\n        ret (sr/register-restore base {:k [frame] :deliver {:deliver :return} :value 9})]\n    (is (= {1 nil 0 false} (:window rd)))\n    (is (= {1 nil 2 9} (:window ret)))\n    (is (= {:segment -1 :pc 3} (:control ret)))\n    (is (nil? (:k ret)))\n    (is (= :deliver (:rule (error-data #(sr/register-restore base {} 1)))))))\n\n\n(deftest free-environment-retention\n  (let [initial {'x 1}\n        ast (corpus/tail (corpus/app (corpus/lam '[x] (corpus/v 'x)) (corpus/lit 2)))\n        machine (parity/register-machine ast {:env initial})\n        states (take-while (complement vm/halted?) (iterate vm/step machine))\n        result (vm/run machine)]\n    (is (= initial (:free-env machine)))\n    (is (= {} (:free-env (sr/create-vm))))\n    (is (every? #(= initial (:free-env %)) states))\n    (is (= 2 (vm/value result)))\n    (is (= {'x 2} (:env result)))\n    (is (= initial (:free-env result)))\n    (is (some #(= initial %) (:values (module/gc-roots result))))\n    (is (= initial (:free-env (vm/reset result))))\n    (is (= initial (:free-env (vm/eval result nil))))\n    (is (= initial (:free-env (sr/attach-image result (golden :literal) code/contract))))\n    (is (= initial (:free-env (sr/load-vector result (golden :literal) code/contract))))\n    (let [restored (sr/register-restore result\n                                        {:segment (:program machine) :pc 0\n                                         :env {'x 3} :window {} :k nil\n                                         :deliver {:deliver :rd :rd 0}}\n                                        9)]\n      (is (= {'x 3} (:env restored)))\n      (is (= initial (:free-env restored))))))\n\n\n(deftest create-vm-test\n  (let [machine (sr/create-vm {:make-stream tu/make-stream\n                              :capability-secret tu/secret})]\n    (is (contains? (:resources machine) vm/call-in-stream-key))\n    (is (contains? (:resources machine) vm/call-out-stream-key))\n    (is (contains? (:resources machine) vm/call-out-cursor-key))\n    (is (= {} (:code machine)))\n    (is (nil? (vm/control machine)))\n    (is (nil? (vm/continuation machine)))\n    (is (vm/halted? machine))\n    (is (= {} (vm/environment machine))))\n  (is (some? (error-data #(sr/create-vm {:in-stream :anything})))))\n\n\n(deftest arithmetic-test\n  (is (= 3 (vm/value (vm/run (parity/register-machine\n                              (corpus/app (corpus/v '+) (corpus/lit 1) (corpus/lit 2)))))))\n  (is (= 12 (vm/value (vm/run (parity/register-machine\n                               (corpus/app (corpus/v '*)\n                                           (corpus/app (corpus/v '+) (corpus/lit 1) (corpus/lit 2))\n                                           (corpus/lit 4))))))))\n\n\n(deftest closure-call-test\n  (let [result (vm/run (parity/register-machine\n                        (corpus/app (corpus/lam '[x] (corpus/tail (corpus/app (corpus/v '+) (corpus/v 'x) (corpus/lit 1))))\n                                    (corpus/lit 10))))]\n    (is (= 11 (vm/value result)))\n    (is (vm/halted? result))\n    (is (nil? (vm/continuation result))))\n  (is (= 15 (vm/value (vm/run (parity/register-machine\n                               (corpus/app\n                                 (corpus/lam '[y]\n                                             (corpus/tail\n                                               (corpus/app (corpus/lam '[x] (corpus/app (corpus/v '+) (corpus/v 'x) (corpus/v 'y)))\n                                                           (corpus/lit 5))))\n                                 (corpus/lit 10))))))))\n\n\n(deftest under-arity-call-binds-missing-param-to-nil-test\n  (is (nil? (vm/value (vm/run (parity/register-machine\n                               (corpus/app (corpus/lam '[y]\n                                                       (corpus/tail\n                                                         (corpus/app (corpus/lam '[x y] (corpus/v 'y))\n                                                                     (corpus/lit 5))))\n                                           (corpus/lit 10))))))))\n\n\n(deftest over-arity-call-drops-extra-args-test\n  (is (= 5 (vm/value (vm/run (parity/register-machine\n                              (corpus/app (corpus/lam '[x] (corpus/v 'x))\n                                          (corpus/lit 5) (corpus/lit 99))))))))\n\n\n(deftest branch-false-test\n  (is (= 1 (vm/value (vm/run (parity/register-machine\n                              (corpus/if-node (corpus/lit true) (corpus/lit 1) (corpus/lit 2)))))))\n  (doseq [test [false nil]]\n    (is (= 2 (vm/value (vm/run (parity/register-machine\n                                (corpus/if-node (corpus/lit test) (corpus/lit 1) (corpus/lit 2)))))))))\n\n\n(deftest store-and-gensym-test\n  (let [result (vm/run (parity/register-machine\n                        (corpus/app (corpus/lam '[ignored] {:type :vm/store-get :key 'a})\n                                    {:type :vm/store-put :key 'a :val 5})))]\n    (is (= 5 (vm/value result)))\n    (is (= 5 (get (vm/store result) 'a))))\n  (is (= :id-0 (vm/value (vm/run (parity/register-machine {:type :vm/gensym :prefix \"id\"})))))\n  (is (= :g-2 (vm/value (vm/run (parity/register-machine\n                                 (corpus/app (corpus/lam '[a b c] (corpus/v 'c))\n                                             {:type :vm/gensym :prefix \"g\"}\n                                             {:type :vm/gensym :prefix \"g\"}\n                                             {:type :vm/gensym :prefix \"g\"})))))))\n\n\n(deftest tail-countdown-test\n  (doseq [[depth tail? frames expected] [[100000 true 1 :resumed]\n                                        [1000 false 1001 :unwound]]]\n    (let [call (corpus/app (corpus/v 'f)\n                           (corpus/app (corpus/v '-) (corpus/v 'n) (corpus/lit 1))\n                           (corpus/v 'f))\n          f (corpus/lam '[n f]\n                        (corpus/if-node (corpus/app (corpus/v '=) (corpus/v 'n) (corpus/lit 0))\n                                        {:type :vm/park}\n                                        (cond-> call tail? corpus/tail)))\n          parked (vm/run (parity/register-machine (corpus/app f (corpus/lit depth) f)))\n          record (vm/value parked)]\n      (is (= :parked-continuation (:type record)))\n      (is (= frames (count (:k record))))\n      (is (= 0 (get (:env record) 'n)))\n      (is (vm/halted? parked))\n      (let [done (vm/run (sr/load-ast parked\n                                     (vm/ast->datoms {:type :vm/resume :parked-id (:id record)\n                                                     :val (corpus/lit expected)})\n                                     vm/ast-contract))]\n        (is (= expected (vm/value done)))\n        (is (vm/halted? done))\n        (is (empty? (:parked done)))))))\n(ns yin.vm.semantic-register.linearize-test\n  (:require [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n            [yin.vm :as vm]\n            [yin.vm.parity-test :as parity]\n            [yin.vm.semantic-register :as sr]\n            [yin.vm.test-utils :as tu]\n            [yin.vm.malformed-rows :as malformed]\n            [yin.vm.semantic-register.code :as code]\n            [yin.vm.semantic-register.corpus :as corpus\n             :refer [app def! if-node lam lit tail v]]\n            [yin.vm.semantic-register.linearize :as linearize]\n            [yin.vm.ucf :as ucf]))\n\n\n(defn- throws-ex-data\n  [thunk]\n  (try (thunk) nil\n       (catch #?(:clj Exception :cljs js/Error :cljd Object) e\n         (or (ex-data e) {}))))\n\n\n(defn- datom-lane\n  [ast]\n  (linearize/project-datoms (vm/ast->datoms ast)))\n\n\n(deftest corpus-is-large-enough\n  (is (<= 25 (count corpus/programs)))\n  (is (= (set (map first corpus/programs)) (set (keys corpus/goldens)))))\n\n\n(deftest row-lane-matches-the-goldens\n  (doseq [[n ast] corpus/programs]\n    (testing n\n      (let [{:keys [vector address]} (linearize/project ast)\n            golden (get corpus/goldens n)]\n        (is (= (:vector golden) vector))\n        (is (= (:address golden) address))))))\n\n\n(deftest datom-lane-matches-the-goldens\n  (doseq [[n ast] corpus/programs]\n    (testing n\n      (let [{:keys [vector address]} (datom-lane ast)\n            golden (get corpus/goldens n)]\n        (is (= (:vector golden) vector))\n        (is (= (:address golden) address))))))\n\n\n(deftest golden-addresses-are-the-code-address-on-this-host\n  (doseq [[n {:keys [vector address]}] corpus/goldens]\n    (testing n\n      (is (= address (ucf/code-address vector))\n          \"the canonical bytes hash identically on every host\"))))\n\n\n(deftest worked-example-is-byte-for-byte-the-design\n  ;; §3.3 item 2: rd(f-call)=0, rd(f)=1, rd(g-call)=2, rd(g)=3, rd(x)=4,\n  ;; rd(y)=5, emitted in evaluation order.\n  (let [expected '[[:var 1 f] [:var 3 g] [:var 4 x] [:call 2 3 [4] false]\n                   [:var 5 y] [:call 0 1 [2 5] false] [:halt 0]]\n        {:keys [vector address]} (linearize/project\n                                   (app (v 'f) (app (v 'g) (v 'x)) (v 'y)))]\n    (is (= expected vector))\n    (is (= (ucf/code-address expected) address))\n    (is (= '[[:var 1 f] [:var 3 g] [:var 4 x] [:call 2 3 [4] false]\n             [:var 5 y] [:call 0 1 [2 5] true] [:halt 0]]\n           (:vector (linearize/project\n                      (tail (app (v 'f) (app (v 'g) (v 'x)) (v 'y))))))\n        \"the tail flag is copied from the AST, nothing else moves\")))\n\n\n(deftest every-production-is-covered\n  (let [ops (set (mapcat (fn [[_ {:keys [vector]}]] (map first vector))\n                         corpus/goldens))]\n    (is (= code/mnemonics ops)\n        \"every §2.3 opcode, hence every §3.1 production, is in the corpus\")))\n\n\n(deftest goldens-are-well-formed\n  (doseq [[n {:keys [vector]}] corpus/goldens]\n    (testing n\n      (is (nil? (code/well-formed? vector))))))\n\n\n(deftest projection-is-deterministic\n  (doseq [[n ast] corpus/programs]\n    (testing n\n      (is (= (linearize/project ast) (linearize/project ast)))\n      (is (= (:vector (linearize/project ast))\n             (:vector (linearize/project\n                        (vm/semantic-bytecode->ast\n                          (vm/ast->semantic-bytecode ast)))))\n          \"rows -> map -> rows projects identically\"))))\n\n\n(deftest saturation-materializes-defaults\n  (is (= (linearize/project {:type :vm/gensym})\n         (linearize/project {:type :vm/gensym, :prefix \"id\"})))\n  (is (= (linearize/project {:type :stream/make})\n         (linearize/project {:type :stream/make, :buffer vm/default-stream-capacity})))\n  (is (= (linearize/project (app (v 'f)))\n         (linearize/project (assoc (app (v 'f)) :tail? false))))\n  (is (= '[[:gensym 0 \"id\"] [:halt 0]]\n         (:vector (linearize/project-datoms\n                    [[-1 :yin/type :vm/gensym 0 0] [-1 :yin/root true 0 0]])))\n      \"the datom lane saturates an omitted prefix\"))\n\n\n(deftest shared-occurrences-expand-positionally\n  (let [ast (get (into {} corpus/programs) :shared-occurrence)\n        bc (vm/ast->semantic-bytecode ast)\n        {:keys [vector provenance]} (linearize/project-rows bc)]\n    (is (= 5 (count (:rows bc)))\n        \"+, g, 1, the root, and one (g 1) row: the shared node is one row\")\n    (is (= [[:call 2 3 [4] false] [:call 5 6 [7] false]]\n           (mapv #(nth vector %) [3 6]))\n        \"the two occurrences of (g 1) lower twice, at two places\")\n    (is (= [[[3 0]] [[3 1]]]\n           (mapv #(last (nth provenance %)) [3 6]))\n        \"the two occurrences carry distinct structural paths\")))\n\n\n(deftest provenance-is-one-row-per-pc\n  (doseq [[n ast] corpus/programs]\n    (testing n\n      (let [bc (vm/ast->semantic-bytecode ast)\n            origin [:source :medium :token 0]\n            {:keys [vector provenance]} (linearize/project-rows bc origin)\n            datoms (vm/ast->datoms ast)\n            entities (set (map first datoms))\n            d (linearize/project-datoms datoms)]\n        (is (= (count vector) (count provenance) (count (:provenance d))))\n        (is (= (range (count vector)) (map first provenance)))\n        (is (every? #(= [origin (:root bc)] (subvec % 1 3)) provenance))\n        (is (every? #(contains? entities (second %)) (:provenance d))\n            \"every datom-lane source names an AST entity\")))))\n\n\n(deftest bodies-are-out-of-line-in-fifo-order\n  (let [{:keys [vector]} (get corpus/goldens :body-queue-order)]\n    (is (= [4 8 10]\n           (keep (fn [t] (when (= :closure (first t)) (nth t 3))) vector))\n        \"main's two lambdas first, then the one discovered inside a body\")\n    (is (= [:halt 0] (nth vector 3)))\n    (is (every? #(= [:return 0] (nth vector %)) [7 9 11]))))\n\n\n(deftest resume-mints-a-definition-less-id\n  (let [{:keys [vector]} (get corpus/goldens :resume-operand)]\n    (is (= [:call 0 1 [2 4] false] (nth vector 4)))\n    (is (not-any? #(= 2 (code/rd %)) vector)\n        \"id 2 is minted by the resume and named only by its consumer\")))\n\n\n(deftest unsupported-and-reserved-nodes-are-refused\n  (is (= :reserved-name\n         (:rule (throws-ex-data\n                  #(linearize/project-datoms\n                     [[-1 :yin/type :variable 0 0]\n                      [-1 :yin/name 'yin/def 0 0]\n                      [-1 :yin/root true 0 0]])))))\n  (is (= :reserved-name\n         (:rule (throws-ex-data\n                  #(linearize/project-datoms\n                     (vm/ast->datoms (lam '[yin/def] (lit 1))))))))\n  (is (some? (throws-ex-data\n               #(linearize/project-datoms\n                  [[-1 :yin/type :vm/store-update 0 0]\n                   [-1 :yin/root true 0 0]]))))\n  (is (some? (throws-ex-data #(linearize/project-datoms [])))))\n\n\n(deftest malformed-row-sets-are-refused\n  (doseq [[n [_expected bc]] malformed/malformed-row-sets]\n    (testing n\n      (is (some? (throws-ex-data #(linearize/project-rows bc)))))))\n\n\n(defn- recording-primitives\n  \"Rule R: a definition is syntax, so nothing can intercept it. `rec`\n   records each definition instead: `(rec 'k (yin/def 'k v))` logs right\n   after the definition runs and returns its value.\"\n  [log]\n  (assoc vm/primitives\n         'rec (fn [key val]\n                (swap! log conj [key val])\n                val)))\n\n\n(defn- rdef!\n  [k val]\n  (app (v 'rec) (lit k) (def! k (if (map? val) val (lit val)))))\n\n\n(def ^:private def-program\n  \"Definitions in operator position, in operands, in an `if` test and both\n   arms, in a closure body run later, in a tail call, and read back\n   through the store.\"\n  (app (if-node (rdef! 'pick true)\n                (lam '[f x]\n                     (tail (app (v 'f)\n                                (rdef! 'c (v 'x))\n                                (rdef! 'd (app (v '+) (v 'b) (lit 1))))))\n                (lam '[f x] (rdef! 'never 0)))\n       (lam '[p q]\n            (if-node (rdef! 'e false)\n                     (rdef! 'never (v 'q))\n                     (tail (app (v '+)\n                                (rdef! 'f (v 'p))\n                                (rdef! 'g (app (v '*) (v 'q) (lit 2)))))))\n       (rdef! 'b (app (v '+) (rdef! 'a 1) (rdef! 'a 2)))))\n\n\n(deftest evaluation-order-matches-the-walker\n  (let [walker-log (atom [])\n        walker (vm/eval (tu/create-vm {:primitives (recording-primitives\n                                                             walker-log)})\n                        def-program)\n        lowered-log (atom [])\n        result (vm/value (vm/run\n                            (sr/load-ast (sr/create-vm {:primitives (recording-primitives lowered-log)})\n                                         (vm/ast->datoms def-program) vm/ast-contract)))]\n    (is (= '[[pick true] [a 1] [a 2] [b 3] [c 3] [d 4] [e false] [f 3] [g 8]]\n           @walker-log)\n        \"the walker's order is the reference\")\n    (is (= @walker-log @lowered-log))\n    (is (= (vm/value walker) result 11))))\n\n\n\n(deftest lower-rows-evaluation-order-matches-the-walker\n  (let [walker-log (atom [])\n        walker (vm/eval (tu/create-vm {:primitives (recording-primitives walker-log)}) def-program)\n        row-log (atom [])\n        result (vm/value (vm/run\n                          (sr/load-vector (sr/create-vm {:primitives (recording-primitives row-log)})\n                                          (:vector (linearize/project-rows (vm/ast->semantic-bytecode def-program)))\n                                          vm/semantic-contract)))]\n    (is (= @walker-log @row-log))\n    (is (= (vm/value walker) result 11))))\n\n\n(deftest literals-are-opaque-data\n  (doseq [type [:vm/store-update :yin/macro-expand]]\n    (let [ast (lit {:type type :key 'k})\n          rows (linearize/project ast)\n          datoms (linearize/project-datoms (vm/ast->datoms ast))]\n      (is (= (:vector rows) (:vector datoms)))\n      (is (= {:type type :key 'k} (nth (first (:vector rows)) 2))))))\n\n\n(deftest host-values-are-rejected-naming-the-node\n  (doseq [value [{:nested [inc]}\n                 (with-meta {:x 1} {:host inc})\n                 {:x (with-meta [1] {:nested {:host inc}})}\n                 (with-meta {:x 1} (with-meta {:k 1} {:host inc}))]]\n    (let [[root datoms] (vm/ast->datoms-with-root (lit value))\n          data (throws-ex-data #(linearize/project-datoms datoms))]\n      (is (= root (:node data)))\n      (is (= :value (:field data)))))\n  (let [data (throws-ex-data #(linearize/project-datoms\n                               (vm/ast->datoms {:type :vm/store-put :key 'k :val #{inc}})))]\n    (is (= :val (:field data)))\n    (is (some? (:node data))))\n  (let [value (with-meta {:x 1} {:line 3})]\n    (is (= {:line 3}\n           (meta (nth (first (:vector (linearize/project-datoms\n                                        (vm/ast->datoms (lit value))))) 2)))))\n  (is (= '+ (nth (first (:vector (linearize/project (v '+)))) 2))))\n\n\n(deftest lower-rows-rejects-incomplete-source-occurrence-identities\n  (let [bc (vm/ast->semantic-bytecode (lit 1))]\n    (doseq [origin [[:source :medium :batch]\n                   [:source :medium :batch -1]\n                   [:source nil :batch 0]\n                   [:source :medium nil 0]\n                   [:expansion :not-an-address]\n                   {:source :medium}]]\n      (is (= :origin (:rule (throws-ex-data #(linearize/project-rows bc origin))))\n          (pr-str origin)))))\n\n\n(def ^:private projection-worked-example\n  \"`((fn [x] (+ x 1)) 10)`, yin.vm.semantic.md §2.7.\"\n  (app (lam '[x] (tail (app (v '+) (v 'x) (lit 1)))) (lit 10)))\n\n\n(def ^:private projection-corpus\n  {:projection-worked-example projection-worked-example,\n   :literal (lit 42),\n   :nil-literal (lit nil),\n   :zero-arity-call (app (lam [] (lit 1))),\n   :nested-lambdas (app (app (lam '[a] (tail (lam '[b] (tail (app (v '+) (v 'a) (v 'b))))))\n                             (lit 1))\n                        (lit 2)),\n   :if-in-tail (app (lam '[n] (if-node (app (v '<) (v 'n) (lit 1))\n                                       (lit :done)\n                                       (tail (app (v '-) (v 'n) (lit 1)))))\n                    (lit 3)),\n   :nested-if (if-node (if-node (lit true) (lit false) (lit true))\n                       (lit :a)\n                       (if-node (lit nil) (lit :b) (lit :c))),\n   :streams {:type :stream/put,\n             :target {:type :stream/make, :buffer 4},\n             :val {:type :stream/next,\n                   :source {:type :stream/cursor,\n                            :source {:type :stream/close,\n                                     :source (lit nil)}}}},\n   :ffi {:type :dao.stream.apply/call, :op :op/echo, :operands [(lit 1) (lit 2)]},\n   :ffi-no-args {:type :dao.stream.apply/call, :op :op/ping, :operands []},\n   ;; §2.4 saturation: both lanes must materialize the same defaults.\n   :default-gensym {:type :vm/gensym},\n   :default-buffer {:type :stream/make},\n   :store-and-control (app (lam '[a b c d]\n                                (tail (app (v 'vector) (v 'a) (v 'b) (v 'c) (v 'd))))\n                           {:type :vm/store-put, :key 'k, :val 5}\n                           {:type :vm/store-get, :key 'k}\n                           {:type :vm/gensym, :prefix \"g\"}\n                           {:type :vm/current-continuation}),\n   :park-resume (if-node (lit false)\n                         {:type :vm/park}\n                         {:type :vm/resume, :parked-id :p1, :val (lit 7)})})\n\n\n\n(defn- path-row\n  \"The row id a §2.5 structural path names, walked through `node`/`nodes`\n   slots by the §2.3 table's row positions (id 0, tag 1, first slot 2):\n   a node slot is its row position, a nodes item a `[position i]` pair —\n   the same convention as `occurrences`' relation, which provenance joins.\"\n  [{:keys [root rows]} path]\n  (reduce (fn [id step]\n            (let [slot (fn [pos] (nth (get rows id) pos))]\n              (if (vector? step)\n                (nth (slot (first step)) (second step))\n                (slot step))))\n          root\n          path))\n\n\n(def ^:private emitting-tag\n  \"The §2.3 tag each directly-emitted mnemonic lowers from; the structural\n   mnemonics (:push :jump :branch-false :halt :return) name no single tag.\"\n  {:const :literal,\n   :var :variable,\n   :closure :lambda,\n   :call :application,\n   :ffi-call :dao.stream.apply/call,\n   :gensym :vm/gensym,\n   :store-get :vm/store-get,\n   :store-put :vm/store-put,\n   :park :vm/park,\n   :resume :vm/resume,\n   :current-continuation :vm/current-continuation,\n   :stream-make :stream/make,\n   :stream-put :stream/put,\n   :stream-cursor :stream/cursor,\n   :stream-next :stream/next,\n   :stream-close :stream/close})\n\n\n(deftest lower-rows-provenance-paths-resolve-to-the-emitting-node\n  (doseq [[label ast] (into projection-corpus (map (fn [[n a _]] [n a]) parity/corpus))]\n    (testing label\n      (let [bc (vm/ast->semantic-bytecode ast)\n            {:keys [vector provenance]} (linearize/project-rows bc)\n            occ (vm/occurrences bc)]\n        (is (= (count vector) (count provenance)))\n        (doseq [[pc _origin root path] provenance\n                :let [mnem (nth (nth vector pc) 0)\n                      id (path-row bc path)]]\n          (is (contains? (:rows bc) id)\n              (str \"path resolves at pc \" pc))\n          (is (contains? occ [root path id])\n              \"the §5.3 join key [root path node] is an occurrence\")\n          (when-let [tag (get emitting-tag mnem)]\n            (is (= tag (nth (get (:rows bc) id) 1))\n                (str mnem \" at pc \" pc \" is emitted by a \" tag))))))))\n\n\n\n(deftest unsupported-nodes-are-rejected-naming-the-node\n  (doseq [type [:vm/store-update :yin/macro-expand]]\n    (let [datoms [[-20 :yin/type type 0 :db/add]\n                  [-21 :yin/type :application 0 :db/add]\n                  [-21 :yin/operator -20 0 :db/add]\n                  [-21 :yin/operands [] 0 :db/add]\n                  [-21 :yin/root true 0 :db/add]]]\n      (is (= {:type type :node -20}\n             (throws-ex-data #(linearize/project-datoms datoms))))))\n  (is (= {:type :no/such :id -20}\n         (throws-ex-data #(linearize/project-datoms\n                            [[-20 :yin/root true 0 :db/add]\n                             [-20 :yin/type :no/such 0 :db/add]])))))\n---\ndescription: Build, lint, test commands, TDD guidelines, and bracket debugging for Clojure, ClojureScript, Node.js, and ClojureDart\n---\n\n# BUILD & TEST\n\n## Commands\n\n```sh\n# Tests (Babashka runner)\nbb test              # All three lanes (JVM, Node, Dart), fast default form: no slow tests\nbb test:all          # Every test on every lane, slow ones included (JVM takes 20+ min)\nbb test:slow         # Only the slow tests, on every lane\n# One lane alone: <task>:clj, <task>:cljs, <task>:cljd\nbb test:clj          # JVM, fast: skips ^:slow (bare `clj -M:test` runs them too)\nbb test:cljs         # Node (shadow-cljs :cljs alias), fast: guarded slow bodies print SKIP\nbb test:cljd         # Dart (needs flutter on PATH), fast: guarded slow bodies print SKIP\nbb test:all:clj      # JVM, no filter: `clojure -M:test`\nbb test:all:cljs     # Node with DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1\nbb test:all:cljd     # Dart with DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1\nbb test:slow:clj     # JVM: `-i :slow` (long-loops-test, ~14 min)\nbb test:slow:cljs    # Node: only the namespaces that use dao.test-slow/guard, DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1\nbb test:slow:cljd    # Dart: only those namespaces' generated tests, DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1\n# Slow tests: tag a deftest ^:slow. The JVM runner then excludes it from `bb test:clj`.\n# Node and Dart have no tag filter, so a .cljc slow test also wraps its body in\n# (dao.test-slow/guard \"name\" (fn [] ...)); it prints SKIP unless DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1.\n# Node and Dart select slow tests by NAMESPACE (derived by grepping `slow/guard`\n# under test/), so the non-slow tests inside those namespaces also run there.\n# On Node, shadow also runs the test namespaces those nine require (about\n# seven more, e.g. lower-portable-test); on Dart only the nine namespaces run.\n# Run test:slow / test:all before a big merge or a commit that touches many parts.\n# Run one Dart lane at a time per machine (the limit is cores and the Flutter cache,\n# not subsystems). On the many-core remote hosts see \"Remote test servers\" below for\n# which lanes may overlap.\n#\n# When to tag a test slow: when it takes more than about 5 s on any lane (the\n# Python e2e tests sit on a ~3 s floor, so their JVM cut is 3.0 s). The\n# default lanes must stay in minutes; 22 JVM tests (0.75% of the suite) were\n# 81% of its test time. Tag it ^:slow on the JVM; if it is a .cljc test, also\n# wrap its body in dao.test-slow/guard so Node and Dart skip it by default. A\n# test that is slow only on Dart (dao.jing.dht-test/unproven-chunks-... takes\n# 72 s there, 3.6 s on the JVM) is a candidate for a speed investigation first.\n# Python slow set (2026-10-06): 65 ^:slow and 15 guard-only tests in the\n# yang.python.antlr e2e, e2e-c1, prelude-parity, safepoint, float-address\n# and int-contract tests; a Python slice landing runs `bb test:sub:clj yang.python --slow`\n# (or `clojure -M:test -i :slow -n <ns>`).\n# While iterating, use the Gate Ladder (see below): G0 iterate via `bb test:sub:clj <own>`\n# or `clojure -M:test -n <ns>`. Do not run the full `bb test` while iterating.\n# At slice checkpoints, run G1 (`bb test:sub <own>`). Before landing a slice, run\n# G2 (`bb test:changed` in the worktree across all three lanes).\n# Full repo-wide `bb test` (G3) is the mandatory landing gate on master after merge.\n# Cross-host bugs show only on Node or Dart, so tri-host verification is mandatory\n# for every gate from G1 upward. Run one lane set at a time per machine to avoid\n# contention (a laptop has 8 cores; the 24- and 48-core remote hosts have room to\n# overlap lanes, see \"Remote test servers\" below).\n# Measured fast-lane times (2026-10-03): bb test about 14 min = JVM 5.5 + Node\n# 3.8 + Dart 4.3, plus builds. test:slow: Node and Dart about 5 min each (mostly\n# compile); the JVM half is estimated at 17 min (long-loops-test alone is 14),\n# not yet run end to end. test:all: JVM 20+ min, also an estimate.\nnpm test             # Node.js tests\n\n# Cross-host peers the JVM lane spawns. `bb test` builds both. A bare\n# `bb test:clj` builds only the Node REPL (it depends on build:yin-repl-node);\n# without build:yin-repl-peer first, the Dart-peer tests skip with a printed notice.\n# Under `bb test:sub` and `bb test:changed`, prerequisites are derived automatically.\nbb build:yin-repl-peer   # Dart exe build/yin-repl-peer (yin.repl R5 pairs)\nbb build:yin-repl-node   # Node REPL target/yin-repl.js; REQUIRED by\n                         # yin.repl.dht-process-test (JVM-to-Node DHT reader,\n                         # and the linker L5 Node reader that requires a module\n                         # by name): `clojure -M:test` without it fails that test\n```\n\n### Changed-only tests: `bb test:changed`\n\n`bb test:changed` (src/dev/affected.clj) runs the fast tests a change can\nreach: the reverse require closure of the files changed since the\nmerge-base with master, plus fixtures that mention a changed resource path,\ntests that walk a changed tree, and each src file's `_test` by convention.\nA walker is a file calling file-seq, fs/glob, fs/list-dir,\nfs/walk-file-tree or .listFiles; each string literal argument of its\nio/file, fs/file, fs/path, fs/glob, java.io.File. or File. calls is a root\n(let-bound roots count), and a change under a root selects it. The three\nlanes run in parallel (logs: target/profile/changed-<lane>.log) after the\nneeded builds. `test:changed:list` shows what and why; `:clj`/`:cljs`/\n`:cljd` run one lane; `--base REF`; `--changed FILE...` (absolute OK; a\ntypo, an empty list or the wrong cwd exits 1). Use it to iterate and to\nland a slice confined to a package. Exit 2 (from :list too) is a wide\nchange (deps.edn bb.edn shadow-cljs.edn mise.toml .cljstyle src/dev/\nantlr/ .clj-kondo/ package*/pubspec*): it runs nothing; run `bb test`,\nas for a change to the core everything requires (yin.vm engine,\ndao.stream, codecs) and before a big merge. Not seen: dynamic loads\n(`requiring-resolve`, `resolve`), paths or walk roots built at run time,\nand spawned programs that changed (target/yin-repl.js, Dart peers).\n\n### Subsystem-first tests: `bb test:sub`\n\n`bb test:sub <subsystem>...` (src/dev/affected.clj) runs the tests belonging to\none or more canonical subsystems (defined in `src/dev/subsystems.edn`). Selection\nis by longest namespace prefix matching.\n\n```sh\nbb test:sub <subsystem>...        # All three lanes in parallel (fast form)\nbb test:sub:clj <subsystem>...    # JVM lane alone\nbb test:sub:cljs <subsystem>...   # Node lane alone\nbb test:sub:cljd <subsystem>...   # Dart lane alone\nbb test:sub:list <subsystem>...   # Show namespaces, builds, Class B seams & dependents; runs nothing\nbb test:sub <subsystem>... --slow # Include slow tests (-i :slow on JVM, DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1 on Node/Dart)\nbb -cp src/dev -m affected-test   # Run affected-test self-tests directly in Babashka\n```\n\n#### Canonical Subsystems (`src/dev/subsystems.edn`)\n\n- **Layer 0 (Core Data & Transport)**: `dao.stream`, `dao.jing`, `dao.data`, `dao.base`\n- **Layer 1 (Space & UI)**: `dao.space`, `dao.gui`, `dao.postgraphics`\n- **Layer 2 (Execution Engine)**: `yin.vm.ucf`, `yin.vm`\n- **Layer 3 (Languages & Interop)**: `yin.repl`, `yang.python`, `yang.base`\n- **Layer 4 (Applications & Demos)**: `demo`, `world`\n- **Infrastructure**: `dev`, `bench`\n\nPrerequisites (`build:yin-repl-peer`, `build:yin-repl-node`, `gen:python-antlr`)\nand lane serialization (`[:clj :cljd]`) are derived purely from text reach of the\nselected namespaces and run automatically when needed.\n\n#### Gate Ladder (docs/design/test.subsystems.md)\n\n1. **G0 Iterate**: Run only the subsystem's JVM lane (`bb test:sub:clj <own>` or `clojure -M:test -n <ns>`).\n2. **G1 Checkpoint**: Run the three-lane subsystem test (`bb test:sub <own>`). Proves the home suite across all three hosts before reporting ready.\n3. **G2 Land**: Run `bb test:changed` in the worktree across all three lanes (plus `bb test:sub <own> --slow` if slow tests are present). Covers dependents across the change (for foundation subsystems like `dao.stream` or `dao.jing`, this correctly runs nearly the full suite).\n4. **G3 Master**: The mandatory landing gate on master after merge, and for any wide change (`bb test`).\n5. **G4 Release**: Full or slow test run before a big release or cross-cutting merge (`bb test:slow` or `bb test:all`), and at each phase boundary of a multi-phase track (owner decision 2026-10-12; see \"Test tiers: quick and slow\" below). G0 to G3 run the quick tier; G4 runs the slow tier.\n\n\nThe linker-over-DHT end-to-end gate (docs/design/yin.vm.linker.dht.md,\nslice L5) is two tests:\n\n- `yin.repl.dht-process-test` (JVM lane only): real `yin.repl.main`\n  processes over real loopback UDP. A JVM publisher with a key file\n  publishes modules by name, and JVM and Node readers require them by\n  name on all four VMs. Plain Clojure in the test JVM takes the same path\n  and checks each section 9 failure as data. Ports are ephemeral, and\n  every wait is bounded. A run takes a few minutes. Run it alone with\n  `clojure -M:test -n yin.repl.dht-process-test`, after\n  `bb build:yin-repl-node`.\n- `yin.vm.linker.dht-end-to-end-test` (all three lanes): the same\n  scenario in process, over the `dao.jing.dht` test mesh seam. Dart's\n  signed-name leg runs here, because no Dart `yin.repl.main` process\n  exists to spawn. `build/yin-repl-peer` is the R5 slice peer, not a\n  REPL.\n\n```sh\n# ClojureScript / shadow-cljs (always via deps.edn :cljs alias, never npx)\nclj -M:cljs -m shadow.cljs.devtools.cli watch <build-id>    # e.g. watch demo\nclj -M:cljs -m shadow.cljs.devtools.cli compile <build-id>  # e.g. compile demo\nclj -M:cljs -m shadow.cljs.devtools.cli release <build-id>  # production release\n\n# ClojureDart\nclj -M:clojuredart:cljd compile\n\n# Linting\nclj -M:kondo --lint <path>\n```\n\nThe Dart `bb` lanes run `src/dev/cljd_agg.clj` (`bb src/dev/cljd_agg.clj\n[--slow-only | --slow-regex]`), not `cljd test`. `--slow-only` runs only the\nnamespaces that use `dao.test-slow/guard` and fails if one has no generated\nDart file. `--slow-regex` prints those namespaces as an anchored alternation\nwith its dots already escaped for an EDN string (bb.edn feeds it to shadow-cljs\n`--config-merge` for `test:slow:cljs`); it is not a ready-to-use regex, and it\nexits 1 when no namespace uses the guard. `flutter test` spends about 7.5 s loading\neach of the ~166 generated `test/cljd-out/**/*_test.dart` files, so the\nscript compiles every test namespace via `clojure -M:clojuredart:cljd compile\n<namespaces>`, writes up to min(8, cores) shard files under `build/cljd-agg/`\n(greedy by file size; each imports its files and calls their `main`), runs\n`flutter test --concurrency N` on the shards, and deletes them. Shards never sit\nunder `test/`, so plain `clojure -M:clojuredart:cljd test` still works. Tests of\ndifferent namespaces share an isolate per shard. Failures stay attributable:\npackage:test names are ns-qualified (`dao.foo-test/bar-test`).\n\n`flutter test`/`cljd test` globs everything under `test/cljd-out/`, and the\ncompile does not prune it when a source file is deleted or renamed. The\naggregated lanes only run namespaces that still exist under `test/`, but a\nstale file can silently pass a plain `cljd test`. Run `rm -rf test/cljd-out`\nbefore relying on that to prove a deletion or rename took effect.\n\n## Test tiers: quick and slow\n\nThe suite has two tiers so that slow tests run less often than quick ones\n(owner decision, 2026-10-12).\n\n- **Quick tier:** every test not tagged `^:slow`. `bb test:clj` or\n  `clojure -M:test -e :slow` on the JVM; the Node and Dart lanes skip the\n  guarded bodies (`dao.test-slow/guard`) unless `DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1`.\n- **Slow tier:** the tagged deftests. `bb test:slow` or\n  `clojure -M:test -i :slow -n <ns>` on the JVM.\n- **The tagging rule** is the one above (\"When to tag a test slow\"): a deftest that\n  takes about 5 s or more run alone. On 2026-10-12 every JVM test namespace and every\n  deftest in the 22 slowest namespaces were timed on a 48-core Linux server, and the\n  **63 deftests at 5 s or more** were tagged: `^:slow` on the deftest, plus the guard\n  wrapper in `.cljc` files. 37 are guarded, 26 are `^:slow` only (`.clj` files and\n  `:clj` reader-conditional branches). Those 22 namespaces now hold **168 slow tests**\n  in all (some were already tagged). Per-test times are not in the repo: measure again\n  with the method below before changing the cut.\n- **Cadence:** the quick tier at every checkpoint (G1) and landing (G2, G3); the slow\n  tier before merging a big change and at each phase boundary of a multi-phase track\n  (the existing G4). There is no nightly run.\n\nMeasured (2026-10-12, origin master plus the tags, Linux servers; see \"Remote test\nservers\" for how to run them):\n\n| Run | Time |\n|---|---|\n| Full JVM lane, one process, before tagging (shiva) | 70 min |\n| Full JVM lane, sharded by subsystem, before tagging (jupiter, 13 shards, 8 at a time) | 46.5 min, set by `yin.repl.python-antlr-test` |\n| **Quick tier, sharded by subsystem (jupiter, same 13 shards)** | **5 min 3 s**, 4055 tests, all shards exit 0; longest shards `yang.python` 253 s and `yin.vm.ucf` 204 s |\n| **Slow tier (shiva, one JVM per namespace, 6 at a time)** | **53 min**, 22 namespaces, 168 tests, all exit 0; longest `yin.repl.python-antlr-test` 3183 s (about 1580 s alone on the laptop) |\n\nThe quick tier has exactly 63 fewer tests than the untagged suite (4118 to 4055).\nSome quick parts are still 25 to 69 s when a namespace is run alone (`e2e-c2`,\n`prelude-parity`, `int-ops`, `holder.driver`, `compose-rows`): many tests each just\nunder the 5 s cut (the Python e2e per-test floor is about 2 to 3 s), not shared setup.\nA lower cut would shrink the quick tier further and move more tests to the slow tier.\n\n**How the per-test times were measured.** To time every deftest of a namespace alone,\nrun it without the test runner's alias main (the `:test` alias's `-m cognitect.test-runner`\notherwise swallows `-e`, and every JVM runs the whole suite):\n\n```sh\nNS=<namespace> clojure -Sdeps '{:aliases {:t {:extra-paths [\"test\"]}}}' -M:t timing.clj\n# timing.clj: require the namespace, for each deftest var that is not ^:slow:\n#   (binding [clojure.test/*test-out* (java.io.StringWriter.)] (clojure.test/test-vars [v]))\n# and print the elapsed nanoseconds. One-off setup (a `use-fixtures :once` or a parser\n# load) is paid by the first test in file order; check before tagging that test alone.\n```\n\n**Sharding the JVM lane by subsystem** (the quick tier; run on a server, see below). The\nshards come from `bb test:sub:list <subsystem>` for the 13 subsystems that hold JVM\ntests, so each subsystem is one JVM; the script also checks that the shards cover every\nJVM test namespace under `test/`:\n\n```sh\n#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# Usage: shard-jvm.sh <clone> [parallel]  -- JVM lane sharded by subsystem (fast tests, -e :slow)\nset -u\nexport PATH=\"$HOME/.local/bin:/snap/bin:$PATH\"\ncd \"$1\" || exit 2\nPAR=\"${2:-8}\"\nmise trust >/dev/null 2>&1\neval \"$(mise env -s bash)\"\nOUT=\"$1/target-ci/shards\"; rm -rf \"$OUT\"; mkdir -p \"$OUT\"\nts() { date +%H:%M:%S; }\necho \"start $(ts) $(git rev-parse --short HEAD) par=$PAR\" | tee \"$OUT/summary.txt\"\nnpm ci --silent >\"$OUT/npm.log\" 2>&1                   && echo \"npm ok $(ts)\" | tee -a \"$OUT/summary.txt\"\nbb build:yin-repl-node >\"$OUT/build-node.log\" 2>&1     && echo \"node repl built $(ts)\" | tee -a \"$OUT/summary.txt\"\nbb gen:python-antlr >\"$OUT/antlr.log\" 2>&1             && echo \"antlr ok $(ts)\" | tee -a \"$OUT/summary.txt\"\nSUBS=\"yang.python yin.repl yin.vm yin.vm.ucf dao.stream dao.jing dao.gui dao.space demo dao.data dao.postgraphics yang.base dao.base\"\n: > \"$OUT/covered.txt\"\nfor s in $SUBS; do\n  bb test:sub:list \"$s\" 2>/dev/null | awk \"/^clj:/{f=1;next} /^[A-Za-z]/{f=0} f{gsub(/ /,\\\"\\\");print}\" > \"$OUT/ns-$s.txt\"\n  cat \"$OUT/ns-$s.txt\" >> \"$OUT/covered.txt\"\n  echo \"$s $(wc -l < \"$OUT/ns-$s.txt\")\" >> \"$OUT/plan.txt\"\ndone\n# coverage: every JVM test namespace under test/ vs the union of the shards\nfind test -type f \\( -name \"*_test.clj\" -o -name \"*_test.cljc\" \\) | sed -e \"s#^test/##\" -e \"s#\\.cljc\\?\\$##\" -e \"s#/#.#g\" -e \"s#_#-#g\" | sort -u > \"$OUT/all.txt\"\nsort -u \"$OUT/covered.txt\" > \"$OUT/covered.sorted\"\ncomm -23 \"$OUT/all.txt\" \"$OUT/covered.sorted\" > \"$OUT/ns-uncovered.txt\"\necho \"all=$(wc -l < $OUT/all.txt) covered=$(wc -l < $OUT/covered.sorted) uncovered=$(wc -l < $OUT/ns-uncovered.txt)\" | tee -a \"$OUT/summary.txt\"\nrun_shard() {\n  s=$1; f=\"$OUT/ns-$s.txt\"; [ -s \"$f\" ] || return 0\n  args=(); while read -r n; do args+=(-n \"$n\"); done < \"$f\"\n  t0=$(date +%s); clojure -M:test -e :slow \"${args[@]}\" >\"$OUT/$s.log\" 2>&1; rc=$?\n  echo \"$s rc=$rc secs=$(( $(date +%s)-t0 )) $(ts) $(grep -E \"^Ran \" \"$OUT/$s.log\" | tail -1)\" | tee -a \"$OUT/summary.txt\"\n}\nexport -f run_shard; export OUT; export -f ts\nprintf \"%s\\n\" $SUBS uncovered | xargs -P \"$PAR\" -I{} bash -c \"run_shard {}\"\necho \"done $(ts)\" | tee -a \"$OUT/summary.txt\"\n```\n\n**The slow tier** runs each tagged namespace on its own JVM, a few at a time:\n\n```sh\n#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# Usage: slow-tier.sh <clone> [parallel] -- the ^:slow tests of the tagged namespaces, one JVM per namespace\nset -u\nexport PATH=\"$HOME/.local/bin:/snap/bin:$PATH\"\ncd \"$1\" || exit 2\nPAR=\"${2:-6}\"\nmise trust >/dev/null 2>&1\neval \"$(mise env -s bash)\"\nOUT=\"$1/target-ci/slowtier\"; rm -rf \"$OUT\"; mkdir -p \"$OUT\"\nrun_ns() {\n  n=$1; t0=$(date +%s)\n  clojure -M:test -i :slow -n \"$n\" > \"$OUT/$n.log\" 2>&1; rc=$?\n  echo \"$n rc=$rc secs=$(( $(date +%s)-t0 )) $(grep -E \"^Ran \" \"$OUT/$n.log\" | tail -1)\" >> \"$OUT/summary.txt\"\n}\nexport -f run_ns; export OUT\necho \"start $(date +%H:%M:%S) $(git rev-parse --short HEAD) par=$PAR\" > \"$OUT/summary.txt\"\nxargs -P \"$PAR\" -I{} bash -c \"run_ns {}\" < \"$HOME/ci/pertest-ns.txt\"\necho \"done $(date +%H:%M:%S)\" >> \"$OUT/summary.txt\"\n```\n\n## Remote test servers: shiva and jupiter\n\nTwo Linux x86_64 servers run the full suite faster than a laptop. Both are\nreached over SSH as `sto` with key authentication, and both have `mise`, `tmux`\nand `git`.\n\n| Host | Cores / RAM | Toolchain state (checked 2026-10-11) |\n|---|---|---|\n| `shiva.stigmergy.systems` | 24 / 62 GB | Complete: java 21, clojure 1.12.4.1602, node 25.6.1, babashka, cljstyle, zprint, flutter 3.47.1-stable. All three lanes run. |\n| `jupiter.stigmergy.systems` | 48 / 62 GB | java 21, clojure, node, zprint; babashka installed with `mise install babashka@latest`; flutter 3.41.9 is NOT the pinned version. Run the JVM and Node lanes here, not Dart. |\n\n**Never test in `~/workspace/datomworld` on either host.** It is a working copy\nthat is behind origin (shiva: 45 commits behind on 2026-10-11) and belongs to its\nowner. Use a scratch clone under `~/ci/` and leave the working copy alone.\n\n### Get the code there: push to origin, never rsync\n\nRsyncing a worktree over the WAN ran at about 150 KB/s (576 MB of tracked files\nwould take about an hour), and an unanchored `--exclude build` also dropped source\ndirectories named `build`, `out` and `target`. Both hosts reach GitHub, so push the\nbranch from the laptop (a feature branch, never master), make one scratch clone on\nthe host from its existing checkout (a local clone takes seconds), and fetch:\n\n```sh\n# once per host: a separate scratch clone, not the working copy\nssh shiva.stigmergy.systems 'set -e; mkdir -p ~/ci; cd ~/workspace/datomworld;\n  URL=$(git remote get-url origin);\n  git clone -q --no-checkout ~/workspace/datomworld ~/ci/datomworld-<name>;\n  cd ~/ci/datomworld-<name>; git remote set-url origin \"$URL\";\n  git fetch -q origin; git checkout -q --detach origin/<branch>'\n```\n\nTo test another branch later, fetch and check it out in the scratch clone with\n`git fetch origin` then `git checkout --detach origin/<branch>`. A branch that\nwas never pushed cannot be tested remotely.\n\n### Activate the toolchain in the right order\n\nA non-interactive `ssh host cmd` does not load the shell profile, so `mise` and its\ntools are not on PATH. In a script, do this in exactly this order, after the `cd`\ninto the clone:\n\n```sh\nexport PATH=\"$HOME/.local/bin:/snap/bin:$PATH\"   # mise: ~/.local/bin on shiva, /snap/bin on jupiter\ncd ~/ci/datomworld-<name>\nmise trust >/dev/null 2>&1                       # trust is per path; a fresh clone is untrusted\neval \"$(mise env -s bash)\"                       # puts the repo-pinned tools on PATH\n```\n\nActivating mise before the `cd` and `mise trust` leaves the repo-pinned tools\n(flutter in particular) off PATH: the Dart lane then dies in seconds with \"Can't\nfind flutter on PATH\", and so does `bb build:yin-repl-peer`.\n\n### Which lanes may overlap (reconciling the one-lane-set rule)\n\n\"One lane set at a time\" and \"one Dart lane at a time\" are per-machine rules about\nCPU: they exist because a laptop has 8 cores. They are not a rule about repos.\n`test.subsystems.md` section 5 item 6 says the same (\"on one machine where\navoidable\"). On shiva (24 cores) and jupiter (48) the cores are not the limit, so\nlanes may overlap, with these limits:\n\n- **JVM and Dart lanes must not share one clone.** `src/dev/affected.clj`\n  (`serialized-pairs`, the `[:clj :cljd]` pair) serializes them whenever a JVM test\n  runs the cljd compiler, and some do (`yin.repl.build-test`,\n  `yin.vm.linker.cross-host-transfer-test`, `dao.stream.ws-project-cross-jvm-test`);\n  the compiler writes the clone's `lib/cljd-out` and `build/`. A second scratch clone\n  gives the Dart lane its own copies, so the two lanes then overlap safely. This is\n  by the design's own reasoning (\"each worktree owns its own `cljd-out`\"), not yet\n  verified by a measured run.\n- **JVM and Node may share a clone.** Node writes `target/` and `.shadow-cljs/`; the\n  JVM lane only reads `target/yin-repl.js`.\n- **One Dart lane per host at a time**, even across clones: the lane shards up to\n  `min(8, cores)` Flutter processes and shares the host's Flutter cache.\n- **Different branches in different clones** are independent, so two branches may\n  run on one host if its cores and RAM allow (62 GB each).\n- Do not treat this as permission to overlap lanes on the laptop.\n\nThe first run on shiva (2026-10-11) overlapped JVM and Dart in one clone before\nthis rule was written down; its results are advisory until repeated with a\nseparate Dart clone.\n\n### The full run\n\nRun long jobs inside `tmux` so the SSH session can drop. The script below does the\nserial prerequisites once, then runs the JVM and Node lanes in the first clone and\nthe Dart lane in a second clone, all concurrently, with the same commands the `bb`\ntasks use (the `bb test` task runs them one after another), and records each\nlane's exit code and seconds. Make the Dart clone the same way as the first, at the\nsame commit, with a name like `~/ci/datomworld-<name>-dart`:\n\n```sh\n#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# ~/ci/run-full.sh <jvm-node-clone> [<dart-clone>]   (omit the second on jupiter: no Dart)\nset -u\nexport PATH=\"$HOME/.local/bin:/snap/bin:$PATH\"\nDART=\"${2:-}\"\ncd \"$1\" || exit 2\nmise trust >/dev/null 2>&1\neval \"$(mise env -s bash)\"\nLOG=\"$1/target-ci\"; mkdir -p \"$LOG\"\nts() { date +%H:%M:%S; }\necho \"start $(ts) $(git rev-parse --short HEAD)\" | tee \"$LOG/summary.txt\"\nnpm ci --silent >\"$LOG/npm.log\" 2>&1               && echo \"npm ok $(ts)\" | tee -a \"$LOG/summary.txt\"\nbb build:yin-repl-node >\"$LOG/build-node.log\" 2>&1 && echo \"node repl built $(ts)\" | tee -a \"$LOG/summary.txt\"\nbb gen:python-antlr >\"$LOG/antlr.log\" 2>&1         && echo \"antlr ok $(ts)\" | tee -a \"$LOG/summary.txt\"\nbb build:yin-repl-peer >\"$LOG/build-peer.log\" 2>&1 && echo \"dart peer built $(ts)\" | tee -a \"$LOG/summary.txt\"  # shiva only\nlane() { name=$1; shift; s=$(date +%s); \"$@\" >\"$LOG/$name.log\" 2>&1; rc=$?\n         echo \"$name rc=$rc secs=$(( $(date +%s)-s )) $(ts)\" | tee -a \"$LOG/summary.txt\"; }\nlane jvm  clojure -M:test -e :slow &\nlane node clj -M:cljs -m shadow.cljs.devtools.cli compile test &\nif [ -n \"$DART\" ]; then                            # shiva only: its own clone (own lib/cljd-out, build/)\n  ( cd \"$DART\" && mise trust >/dev/null 2>&1 && eval \"$(mise env -s bash)\"\n    bb build:yin-repl-peer >\"$LOG/build-peer-dart.log\" 2>&1\n    lane dart bb src/dev/cljd_agg.clj ) &\nfi\nwait\necho \"done $(ts)\" | tee -a \"$LOG/summary.txt\"\n```\n\n```sh\nssh <host> 'tmux new-session -d -s ci-full \"bash -lc \\\"~/ci/run-full.sh ~/ci/datomworld-<name> ~/ci/datomworld-<name>-dart > ~/ci/run-full.out 2>&1\\\"\"'\n```\n\nWatch it: `ssh <host>`, then `tmux attach -t ci-full` (detach with `Ctrl-b d`; do not\npress Ctrl-C inside it), or `tail -f ~/ci/datomworld-<name>/target-ci/{jvm,node,dart}.log`\nand `cat .../summary.txt` (all logs and the summary are in the first clone). The session's own output is empty by design: the lanes\nwrite to the logs. The JVM lane uses `-e :slow`, so it skips `^:slow` tests, like\n`bb test:clj`. For the slow set use `-i :slow` (or `bb test:slow`); the slow C4\nscanner row took about 11-19 minutes on the JVM and about 79 minutes on Node\n(measured 2026-10-11).\n\n### Known differences from the laptop\n\n- **`dao.stream.datagram.dart-test/refusals-and-lifecycle-events` fails on Linux.**\n  The assertion \"a bind on a taken port deposits bind-failed\" gets no `bind-failed`\n  event. A second UDP bind on a taken port evidently behaves differently on Linux\n  than on macOS (inferred, not confirmed). The test is in `dao.stream`, which the\n  semantic-register slices do not touch: treat it as a known Linux-only failure,\n  not a regression, until it is fixed or guarded.\n- A JVM lane started before the Dart peer is built skips the Dart-peer tests with a\n  printed notice. The script builds the peer first so they run.\n- Both hosts run other work (a QEMU guest and rustdesk on shiva); idle load is\n  under 1, but timings are not a clean benchmark.\n\n### Measured times (first runs, 2026-10-11, commit 84c7c9b7, all lanes concurrent)\n\nShiva, Dart lane: 1054 s (17.5 min) cold, with the JVM and Node lanes running beside\nit, against about 9 minutes on the 8-core laptop run alone. Prerequisites (`npm ci`,\nNode REPL, ANTLR) took about 30 s; the Dart peer 91 s. JVM and Node lane times are\nnot recorded yet: fill them in from `summary.txt` after a completed run. Running the\nlanes concurrently on one host did not make the Dart lane faster, so count on the\nextra cores and a free laptop, and measure before relying on a speedup.\n\n## Testing Philosophy & TDD\n\nWrite tests before implementing features (TDD).\n\nTests define the contract and expected behavior. Implementation follows from the tests, not the other way around.\n\nWhen implementing a feature or fix:\n1. **Red phase**: Write the test first — define what should happen.\n2. **Green phase**: Implement the minimum code to pass the test.\n3. **Refactor phase**: Refactor if needed while keeping tests green.\n\nThis ensures code is testable by design and implementation matches actual requirements.\n\n## Debugging Malformed CLJ / EDN / CLJS\n\nA single missing bracket can silently break an entire file. The compiler may still succeed, with subsequent forms nesting inside the broken one.\n\n1. **Run clj-kondo first**:\n   ```sh\n   clj -M:kondo --lint path/to/file.cljs\n   ```\n\n2. **If clj-kondo reports a mismatch, write a bracket-tracing script**:\n   Do NOT try to eyeball-count brackets. Track a stack of `(char, line, col)` for every opener. Handle: string literals, escaped chars, and `;;` line comments.\n\n3. **Fix one bracket at a time, re-run checker after each fix**:\n   Common patterns:\n   - Hiccup vector missing `]` causes siblings to become extra arguments.\n   - `defn`/`let` missing `)` causes subsequent top-level forms to nest inside.\n   - Both can coexist while total bracket count is zero-sum.\n\n4. **After brackets balance**, rerun `clj-kondo`, then rebuild with `clj -M:cljs -m shadow.cljs.devtools.cli compile <build>`.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,115p' test/yin/vm/semantic_register/vm_test.cljc\nsed -n '95,155p' test/yin/vm/semantic_register/linearize_test.cljc\ngit show HEAD:test/yin/vm/semantic_test.cljc | rg -n -A24 'deftest reset-test'\ncat collab/1792056067234-engineer-8f3b.report.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,115p' test/yin/vm/semantic_register/vm_test.cljc\nsed -n '95,155p' test/yin/vm/semantic_register/linearize_test.cljc\ngit show HEAD:test/yin/vm/semantic_test.cljc | rg -n -A24 'deftest reset-test'\ncat collab/1792056067234-engineer-8f3b.report.md\"","aggregated_output":"(ns yin.vm.semantic-register.vm-test\n  (:require [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n            [yin.vm :as vm]\n            [yin.vm.test-utils :as tu]\n            [yin.vm.engine :as engine]\n            [yin.vm.module :as module]\n            [yin.vm.values :as values]\n            [yin.vm.semantic-register :as sr]\n            [yin.vm.semantic-register.analysis :as analysis]\n            [yin.vm.semantic-register.code :as code]\n            [yin.vm.semantic-register.code-test :as code-test]\n            [yin.vm.semantic-register.corpus :as corpus]\n            [yin.vm.semantic-register.parity-test :as parity]))\n\n\n(defn error-data\n  [f]\n  (try (f) nil (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) e (ex-data e))))\n\n\n(defn step-n\n  [machine n]\n  (nth (iterate vm/step machine) n))\n\n\n(defn golden\n  [label]\n  (:vector (get corpus/goldens label)))\n\n\n(defn load-golden\n  [label opts]\n  (sr/load-vector (sr/create-vm opts) (golden label) code/contract))\n\n\n(deftest stamp-before-rules\n  (doseq [[stamp rule] [[nil :contract-missing] [\"v3\" :contract-mismatch]]]\n    (is (= rule (:rule (error-data #(sr/load-vector (sr/create-vm) [] stamp)))))))\n\n\n(deftest loader-refusals-are-the-validators\n  (doseq [[item expected vector] code-test/refusals]\n    (testing (str item \" \" vector)\n      (is (= expected (:defect (error-data #(sr/load-vector (sr/create-vm) vector code/contract))))))))\n\n\n(deftest image-shape\n  (let [machine (load-golden :worked-example {}) seg (:program machine)\n        image (get (:code machine) seg)]\n    (is (= #{:vector :address :bodies :analysis :segment :length} (set (keys image))))\n    (is (= (golden :worked-example) (:vector image)))\n    (is (= (analysis/analyze (:vector image)) (:analysis image)))\n    (is (= (:address (get corpus/goldens :worked-example)) (:address image)))\n    (is (= seg (get (:code-aliases machine) (:address image))))\n    (is (= {:segment seg :pc 0} (vm/control machine)))\n    (is (= {} (:window machine)))\n    (is (nil? (:k machine)))\n    (is (= 7 (:length image)))\n    (is (not (contains? machine :stack)))))\n\n\n(deftest segment-ids\n  (let [a (load-golden :literal {}) floor (vm/loaded-code-floor (:code a))\n        b (sr/load-vector a (golden :variable) code/contract)\n        reload (sr/load-vector b (golden :literal) code/contract {:id 999})]\n    (is (< (:program b) floor))\n    (is (= (:program a) (:program reload)))\n    (is (= (:code b) (:code reload)))\n    (is (re-find #\"already holds different code\"\n                 (try (sr/load-vector a (golden :variable) code/contract {:id (:program a)}) \"\"\n                      (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) e (ex-message e)))))))\n\n\n(deftest attach-load-ast-and-reset\n  (let [a (step-n (load-golden :literal {}) 1)\n        b (sr/attach-image a (golden :variable) code/contract)\n        fields [:control :program :env :window :k :value :halted? :blocked? :parked :wait-set :ready-queue]\n        reset (vm/reset b)\n        ast-loaded (sr/load-ast (sr/create-vm) (vm/ast->datoms (corpus/lit 42)) vm/ast-contract)]\n    (is (= (select-keys a fields) (select-keys b fields)))\n    (is (= 2 (count (:code b))))\n    (is (= b (sr/attach-image b (golden :variable) code/contract)))\n    (is (= {} (:window reset)))\n    (is (nil? (:value reset)))\n    (is (= (:code b) (:code reset)))\n    (is (= 42 (vm/value (vm/run ast-loaded))))\n    (is (= :contract-mismatch (:rule (error-data #(sr/load-ast (sr/create-vm) [] \"bad\")))))\n    (is (some? (error-data #(vm/eval a (corpus/lit 1)))))\n    (is (= 42 (vm/value (vm/eval a nil))))))\n\n\n(deftest one-step-one-write\n  (let [f vector machine (load-golden :worked-example {:env {'f f 'g inc 'x 1 'y 2}})\n        after (vm/step machine)]\n    (is (= {:segment (:program machine) :pc 1} (vm/control after)))\n    (is (= {1 f} (:window after)))))\n\n\n(deftest return-frame-shape\n  (let [machine (load-golden :worked-example {:env {'f vector 'x nil 'y 2}})\n        seg (:program machine)\n        c (values/closure (:owner machine) {:type :closure :params '[z] :segment seg :entry 0 :env {}})\n        machine (assoc-in machine [:env 'g] c)\n        before (step-n machine 3) after (vm/step before)\n        frame (peek (:k after))\n        saved (select-keys (:window before) (analysis/saved (get-in before [:code seg :analysis]) 4 2))]\n    (is (= 3 (get-in before [:control :pc])))\n    (is (= {:type :return :segment seg :pc 4 :env (:env before) :window saved :rd 2} frame))\n    (is (= {1 vector} (:window frame)))\n    (is (= 2 (:rd frame)))\n    (is (= {} (:window after)))))\n\n\n(deftest tail-call-grows-no-frame\n  (let [ast (corpus/app (corpus/lam '[x] (corpus/tail (corpus/app (corpus/lam '[y] (corpus/v 'y)) (corpus/v 'x)))) (corpus/lit 7))\n\n\n(deftest saturation-materializes-defaults\n  (is (= (linearize/project {:type :vm/gensym})\n         (linearize/project {:type :vm/gensym, :prefix \"id\"})))\n  (is (= (linearize/project {:type :stream/make})\n         (linearize/project {:type :stream/make, :buffer vm/default-stream-capacity})))\n  (is (= (linearize/project (app (v 'f)))\n         (linearize/project (assoc (app (v 'f)) :tail? false))))\n  (is (= '[[:gensym 0 \"id\"] [:halt 0]]\n         (:vector (linearize/project-datoms\n                    [[-1 :yin/type :vm/gensym 0 0] [-1 :yin/root true 0 0]])))\n      \"the datom lane saturates an omitted prefix\"))\n\n\n(deftest shared-occurrences-expand-positionally\n  (let [ast (get (into {} corpus/programs) :shared-occurrence)\n        bc (vm/ast->semantic-bytecode ast)\n      